<reference id="scenario_2_inline_equation" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>Scenario 2 — Inline equation</title>
   <shortdesc>Consider an equation added inline with a paragraph.</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <keyword>equation</keyword>
        <keyword>MathML</keyword>
        <keyword>Inline</keyword>
        <keyword>DITA</keyword>
        <keyword>Scenario</keyword>
        <keyword>paragraph</keyword>
        <indexterm>equation</indexterm>
        <indexterm>MathML</indexterm>
        <indexterm>Inline</indexterm>
      </keywords>
      <prodinfo>
        <prodname></prodname>
      </prodinfo>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
   <refbody>
      <section>
         <p>Consider an equation added inline with a paragraph.</p>
         <table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
            <title>Inline equation within paragraph</title>
            <tgroup cols="2">
               <colspec colname="c1"/>
               <colspec colname="c2"/>
               <thead>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <b>.docx Style / Input</b>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <b>DITA Output</b>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </thead>
               <tbody>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <b>[Normal]:</b> The formula <b>[Equation object: E = mc²]</b> defines energy equivalence.</entry>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock id="codeblock_p25_dmr_kkc">
&lt;p>
  The formula
  &lt;math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
    &lt;mrow>
      &lt;mi>E&lt;/mi>
      &lt;mo>=&lt;/mo>
      &lt;mi>m&lt;/mi>
      &lt;msup>
        &lt;mi>c&lt;/mi>
        &lt;mn>2&lt;/mn>
      &lt;/msup>
    &lt;/mrow>
  &lt;/math>
  defines energy equivalence.
&lt;/p></codeblock>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </tbody>
            </tgroup>
         </table>
<p><b>Result</b>: The converter processes supported Word equation objects and converts them into MathML elements embedded within the DITA topic.</p>
<note type="note"> The generated MathML structure may vary depending on the converter implementation
            and the DITA schema or MathML domain used by the publishing environment. Validate
            mathematical output after conversion to ensure rendering accuracy in HTML, PDF, and
            downstream publishing systems.</note>
   </section>
   </refbody>
